# Wave W17-V (Route 208): rest pine — a rest pine in warm foothill greens, tiered and broad, its crown easy in the still air below the south door with the highlight lifted clear of the turf, on rest turf (ground baked in). Route 208’s own tree — split from Route 207’s climb pine beside it by crown warmth (ease vs effort, the same mountain seen from its two doors’ roads) and from Route 211’s bluff-top pine by register (rest meadow vs meditation bluff).
